afk: the cost status-line segment shows the session-sticky Anthropic
OAuth account email, with a one-shot startup warm-up so it resolves
right after launch.

Motivation: with multiple Anthropic OAuth accounts rotating
(session-sticky, usage-ranked), the status line should name the account
this session is billing against. Before the first request no sticky
attribution exists, so a plain identity lookup would name the first
stored account — which selection may not pick.

Depends on omp-anthropic-weekly-reset-priority.patch for
getOAuthAccountIdentity's `sessionStickyOnly` option.

What must survive a rebase:
- segments.ts costSegment appends `theme.fg("muted", email)` (sanitized,
  truncated to TRUNCATE_LENGTHS.SHORT = 40 cols) after the billing
  parts, anthropic provider only, via a sessionStickyOnly identity
  lookup — nothing is shown until the session is actually routed. The
  structured `describe()` view of the cost segment carries the same email
  as a trailing muted span.
- component.ts #warmOAuthAttribution: one-shot per provider+session,
  runs only when an OAuth identity exists and no sticky attribution is
  recorded yet; fire-and-forget getApiKey (with modelId when known),
  then a repaint via #onBranchChange.
- The warm-up call sits in #buildSegmentContext (next to
  refreshUsageInBackground) so every status-line layout — box, the 18.x
  default powerline band, and the plain variants — triggers it.

Rebase notes (17.2.14 -> 18.0.11): the cost segment was restructured
upstream (formatSpend, nerd-font subscription icon, premium requests,
lazy advisor-subscription probe); the email append re-landed after the
new billingParts assembly. The warm-up call followed the render context
builder into #buildSegmentContext.

Rebase notes (18.1.13 -> 18.2.10): the status line moved to
@oh-my-pi/pi-tui/status-line behind a StatusLineHost seam, so the
component can no longer reach authStorage. Re-cut across the seam:
- host.ts: StatusLineSession gains sessionId; StatusLineHost gains two
  optional capabilities, attributedAccount (sticky-only identity) and
  warmAccountAttribution (getApiKey).
- coding-agent modes/status-line-host.ts implements both.
- component.ts #warmOAuthAttribution keeps the one-shot key logic (armed
  only once an OAuth identity exists, skipped when already attributed)
  and #buildSegmentContext puts `accountEmail` on the SegmentContext
  (anthropic only); segments.ts costSegment appends it.
- Tests re-cut: status-line-cost-account.test.ts drives renderSegment
  via ctx.accountEmail; status-line-auth-warmup.test.ts drives the real
  statusLineHost against a stub authStorage.

Rebased 18.2.10 -> 18.6.0: upstream moved AuthStorage to namespaced
APIs, so the host now calls `authStorage.oauth.identity(..., {
sessionStickyOnly: true })` (option added by the weekly-reset patch) and
`authStorage.keys.get(...)` for the warm-up; the warm-up test stub
mirrors that shape. Upstream added a structured `describe()` view per
segment (spans for the native terminal renderer); the cost segment's
email is applied there too, sharing one sanitize/truncate helper
(attributedAccountEmail) with render(). component.ts/host.ts/types.ts
re-landed unchanged in substance at the moved offsets.

